# 基础词 Unit26
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2023红宝书考研英语词汇-基础词
# 描述: 基础词Unit26核心词汇

{{humor}}{/ˈhjuːmər/}}n. 幽默；心情}}{{He has a great sense of humor and makes everyone laugh.}}
{{hunger}}{/ˈhʌŋɡər/}}n. 饥饿；渴望}}{{Millions of people around the world suffer from hunger.}}
{{hunt}}{/hʌnt/}}v. 打猎；搜索；n. 打猎}}{{The lions hunt in groups to catch larger prey.}}
{{hurry}}{/ˈhʌri/}}v. 赶紧；n. 匆忙}}{{We need to hurry or we will miss the train.}}
{{hurt}}{/hɜːrt/}}v. 伤害；n. 伤痛}}{{She hurt her ankle while playing basketball.}}
{{ideal}}{/aɪˈdɪəl/}}adj. 理想的；n. 理想}}{{This is an ideal place for a family vacation.}}
{{identify}}{/aɪˈdentɪfaɪ/}}v. 识别；鉴定}}{{The witness was able to identify the suspect.}}
{{identity}}{/aɪˈdentəti/}}n. 身份；特征}}{{The police are trying to confirm the identity of the victim.}}
{{ignore}}{/ɪɡˈnɔːr/}}v. 忽视；不理睬}}{{You should not ignore the warning signs.}}
{{ill}}{/ɪl/}}adj. 生病的；n. 疾病}}{{She has been ill with the flu for several days.}}
{{illegal}}{/ɪˈliːɡl/}}adj. 非法的；违法的}}{{It is illegal to drive without a license.}}
{{illustrate}}{/ˈɪləstreɪt/}}v. 说明；给…配插图}}{{The teacher used diagrams to illustrate the concept.}}
{{image}}{/ˈɪmɪdʒ/}}n. 图像；形象；印象}}{{The company is working hard to improve its public image.}}
{{imagine}}{/ɪˈmædʒɪn/}}v. 想象；设想}}{{Can you imagine living on another planet?}}
{{immediate}}{/ɪˈmiːdiət/}}adj. 立即的；直接的}}{{The doctor ordered immediate treatment for the patient.}}
{{immigrant}}{/ˈɪmɪɡrənt/}}n. 移民；adj. 移入的}}{{The city has a large immigrant population.}}
{{impact}}{/ˈɪmpækt/}}n. 影响；冲击；v. 影响}}{{The new policy had a significant impact on the economy.}}
{{imply}}{/ɪmˈplaɪ/}}v. 暗示；意味}}{{His silence implied that he disagreed with the decision.}}
{{import}}{/ɪmˈpɔːrt/}}v. 进口；n. 进口品}}{{The country imports most of its oil from the Middle East.}}
{{importance}}{/ɪmˈpɔːrtns/}}n. 重要性；重要}}{{Education is of great importance to a country's development.}}
{{impose}}{/ɪmˈpəʊz/}}v. 强加；征收}}{{The government imposed new taxes on luxury goods.}}
{{impress}}{/ɪmˈpres/}}v. 使印象深刻；铭记}}{{Her presentation impressed everyone at the conference.}}
{{improve}}{/ɪmˈpruːv/}}v. 改善；提高}}{{She is working hard to improve her English skills.}}
{{incident}}{/ˈɪnsɪdənt/}}n. 事件；事故}}{{The police investigated the incident thoroughly.}}
{{include}}{/ɪnˈkluːd/}}v. 包括；包含}}{{The price includes breakfast and dinner.}}
{{income}}{/ˈɪnkʌm/}}n. 收入；所得}}{{His monthly income is enough to support his family.}}
{{increase}}{/ɪnˈkriːs/}}v./n. 增加；增长}}{{The population of the city has increased rapidly.}}
{{incredible}}{/ɪnˈkredəbl/}}adj. 难以置信的；惊人的}}{{The view from the mountain top was incredible.}}
{{indeed}}{/ɪnˈdiːd/}}adv. 的确；确实}}{{It is indeed a great honor to receive this award.}}
{{independence}}{/ˌɪndɪˈpendəns/}}n. 独立；自主}}{{The country gained independence in 1947.}}
{{independent}}{/ˌɪndɪˈpendənt/}}adj. 独立的；自主的}}{{She is an independent woman who makes her own decisions.}}
{{indicate}}{/ˈɪndɪkeɪt/}}v. 表明；指示}}{{The research results indicate a positive trend.}}
{{individual}}{/ˌɪndɪˈvɪdʒuəl/}}adj. 个人的；n. 个人}}{{Each individual has the right to express their opinion.}}
{{industry}}{/ˈɪndəstri/}}n. 工业；行业}}{{The tourism industry contributes greatly to the economy.}}
{{infection}}{/ɪnˈfekʃn/}}n. 感染；传染病}}{{Washing your hands frequently helps prevent infection.}}
{{inflation}}{/ɪnˈfleɪʃn/}}n. 通货膨胀；膨胀}}{{High inflation reduces the purchasing power of consumers.}}
{{influence}}{/ˈɪnfluəns/}}n. 影响；v. 影响}}{{Parents have a great influence on their children's development.}}
{{inform}}{/ɪnˈfɔːrm/}}v. 通知；告知}}{{Please inform us of any changes to the schedule.}}
{{initial}}{/ɪˈnɪʃl/}}adj. 最初的；n. 首字母}}{{The initial results of the experiment are very promising.}}
{{initiative}}{/ɪˈnɪʃətɪv/}}n. 主动性；倡议}}{{She took the initiative to organize the charity event.}}
